================================================================================
OVERALL ASSESSMENT
================================================================================

Root Cause of DMS Failures:
----------------------------
The DMS tool consistently failed at the metadata model creation stage with the error:
"No objects were found according to the specified selection rules."

This suggests that the DMS migration project does not have proper access to the source database metadata, or the selection rules are not configured to include the required tables (Products, ProductHistory, ProductStats).

Manual Conversion Quality:
---------------------------
Despite DMS failures, manual conversions are straightforward because:
1. Most SQL features used (CTEs, window functions, CASE) are standard SQL
2. PostgreSQL has excellent SQL standard compliance
3. Main differences are syntactic (parameters, date functions, identity retrieval)

Conversion Patterns Applied Consistently:
------------------------------------------
1. Parameters: @Name → $N (positional)
2. Date function: GETDATE() → CURRENT_TIMESTAMP
3. Identity: SCOPE_IDENTITY() → RETURNING clause
4. Variable assignment: SELECT @Var = Col → SELECT Col INTO v_Var
5. Transactions: Managed by ADO.NET, not embedded in SQL

Recommendations:
----------------
1. All converted statements should be tested against an actual PostgreSQL database
2. The DMS migration project configuration should be reviewed to ensure proper metadata access
3. Consider re-attempting DMS conversion after fixing metadata access issues
4. All manual conversions follow PostgreSQL best practices and should be functionally equivalent

